e deepest closest resection margin  Immediately adjacent to the lateral surgical scar is an ill defined  yellowish tan  stellate lesion  measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  There are focal areas of hemorrhage within this lesion and the lesion is approximately 1 0cm from the closest resection margin  In the remaining parenchyma are multiple small nodules in the upper outer quadrant  each measuring approximately 0 5cm in greatest dimension  The axillary tissue is examined for lymph nodes  SECTION CODE  AandB  representative sections of the lesion  immediately adjacent to the medial scar with representative skin C DandE  representative sections of the medial lesion with representative sections of the deep resection margin F  representative section of the lesion adjacent to the lateral scar with skin and lateral resection margin G  representative section of the lateral lesion  with deep resection margin H  representative section of the lateral lesion I  representative section of the nodular areas J  representative sections of five possible lymph nodes  the largest measuring 0 5cm in greatest dimension K  representative section of five possible lymph nodes  the largest measuring 0 6cm in greatest dimension L  representative sections of two possible lymph nodes  the largest measuring 1 0cm in greatest dimension  Resident  KEITH KWAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Mastectomy.
