urface is inked yellow  The specimen is sectioned vertically from right to left to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm biopsy cavity with a wall that is tan to tan pink  focally granular  coming focally within 0 1cm of the inked resection margin  Granular tissue from the biopsy cavity wall abuts the resection margin in a number of locations  Over 95  of the specimen is submitted from medial to lateral as A through Z as follows  A  medial end  en face  red ink indicates inferior portion  B D F H J L N P R T V X  superior  from medial to lateral  C E G I K M O Q S U W Y  inferior  from medial to lateral  Z  lateral margin  en face  Designated  Left axillary node tissue   is a 40 gm  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm in maximum dimension axillary lymph node dissection  Nodes are submitted as AA through EE  Designated  Additional axillary tissue   is a 0 3cm in diameter node and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm piece of fatty tissue  submitted in toto as FF  In addition there is a 0 2cm tan to fatty piece of tissue  submitted in toto as GG  Resident  James Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  L Celeste Robb Nicholson  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY TISSUE   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY   report_end  , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
