e  tan white chalky material  The remaining parenchyma consists of tan yellow lobulated unremarkable fibrofatty tissue with no masses or lesions grossly appreciated  At the lateral aspect no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire 6 o clock cavity to include the closest anterior margin and the exposed posterior aspect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant tissue that may represent lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  report_end  , Mastectomy.
