with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 AUG 94 at 16 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm tan yellow  fibrofatty piece of tissue with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm tan skin ellipse with a 2 5cm in diameter dark brown inverted nipple as well as a 3 5cm in length well healed surgical scar  4 0cm away from the nipple and 0 7cm away from the closest margin  The specimen is not oriented  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of irregular  tan fibrosis and fat necrosis present  2 0cm deep to the surgical scar and 1 0cm away from the closest surgical margin  There is a 1 5cm in diameter irregular  fibrotic area  10 0cm away from the previous biopsy site and 0 5cm away from the closest surgical margin  SECTION CODE  A  nipple  B  surgical scar  C  biopsy site with adjacent surgical margin  D G  rest of biopsy site  H J  irregular fibrotic area  10 0cm away from biopsy site  Resident  Horace C  Wu  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  William Thomas Caine  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Mastectomy.
