Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEVERAL NODULES  THE LARGEST REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumors  The lobular carcinoma cells do not stain for E cadherin  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   MASTECTOMY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 OF 4 LYMPH NODES  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received unfixed   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a suture designating the 12 o clock position  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 11 2 cm irregular portion of tan skin with a 4 6 cm well healed linear scar at the 8 to 9 o clock position and a 2 5 cm well healed scar located more laterally  The anterior margin is inked blue  and the posterior margin is inked black  The breast contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5 cm cavity  which is below the 8 to 9 o clock scar  The borders of the cavity are firm and hemorrhagic and contain focal yellow areas of chalky adipose tissue and two metal clips  The cavity extends to the posterior margin and comes to 2cm of the anterior margin  Beneath the second scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6 cm ill defined  firm area containing focal chalky yellow adipose tissue and one clip  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7 cm well circumscribed  firm  tan to white nodule located 0 5cm superior to the cavity  which comes to 2 3cm of the posterior margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  well circumscribed  tan pink nodule in the upper outer quadrant  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to nearest posterior margin  to include defect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm  well circumscribed nodule  superior to cavity  to include nearest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm area subjacent to the second most lateral scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant nodule  bisected  possible lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant tissue which may represent lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  report_end  , Mastectomy.
